"400\" y=\"123\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#67E8F9\" font-size=\"10\" font-family=\"ui-monospace,monospace\" font-weight=\"700\">Ingress Controller</text>\n  <text x=\"400\" y=\"133\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"rgba(103,232,249,0.5)\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">nginx / Traefik — TLS termination</text>\n  <text x=\"400\" y=\"158\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"rgba(0,212,255,0.35)\" font-size=\"9\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"700\">WORKER NODES</text>\n  <rect x=\"20\" y=\"164\" width=\"230\" height=\"130\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"rgba(0,212,255,0.04)\" stroke=\"rgba(0,212,255,0.18)\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/>\n  <text x=\"135\" y=\"180\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"rgba(0,212,255,0.45)\" font-size=\"9\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"700\">Node 1 — m5.xlarge</text>\n  <rect x=\"32\" y=\"186\" width=\"96\" height=\"24\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"rgba(0,212,255,0.1)\" stroke=\"rgba(0,212,255,0.25)\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n  <text x=\"80\" y=\"202\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#67E8F9\" font-size=\"9\" font-family=\"ui-monospace,monospace\">api-pod (250m)</text>\n  <rect x=\"138\" y=\"186\" width=\"96\" height=\"24\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"rgba(0,212,255,0.1)\" stroke=\"rgba(0,212,255,0.25)\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n  <text x=\"186\" y=\"202\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#67E8F9\" font-size=\"9\" font-family=\"ui-monospace,monospace\">api-pod (250m)</text>\n  <rect x=\"32\" y=\"218\" width=\"96\" height=\"24\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"rgba(123,47,255,0.1)\" stroke=\"rgba(123,47,255,0.25)\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n  <text x=\"80\" y=\"234\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#C4B5FD\" font-size=\"9\" font-family=\"ui-monospace,monospace\">worker (500m)</text>\n  <rect x=\"138\" y=\"218\" width=\"96\" height=\"24\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.08)\" stroke=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.2)\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n  <text x=\"186\" y=\"234\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#FCD34D\" font-size=\"9\" font-family=\"ui-monospace,monospace\">unset limits</text>\n  <text x=\"135\" y=\"276\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"rgba(239,68,68,0.55)\" font-size=\"8.5\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">CPU: 4 cores · Memory: 16Gi</text>\n  <text x=\"135\" y=\"288\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"rgba(239,68,68,0.45)\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">idle pods: ~$180/mo wasted</text>\n  <rect x=\"285\" y=\"164\" width=\"230\" height=\"130\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"rgba(0,212,255,0.04)\" stroke=\"rgba(0,212,255,0.18)\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/>\n  <text x=\"400\" y=\"180\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"rgba(0,212,255,0.45)\" font-size=\"9\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"700\">Node 2 — m5.xlarge</text>\n  <rect x=\"298\" y=\"186\" width=\"96\" height=\"24\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"rgba(0,212,255,0.1)\" stroke=\"rgba(0,212,255,0.25)\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n  <text x=\"346\" y=\"202\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#67E8F9\" font-size=\"9\" font-family=\"ui-monospace,monospace\">api-pod (250m)</text>\n  <rect x=\"402\" y=\"186\" width=\"96\" height=\"24\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"rgba(123,47,255,0.1)\" stroke=\"rgba(123,47,255,0.25)\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n  <text x=\"450\" y=\"202\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#C4B5FD\" font-size=\"9\" font-family=\"ui-monospace,monospace\">ml-pod (2000m)</text>\n  <rect x=\"298\" y=\"218\" width=\"200\" height=\"24\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"rgba(52,211,153,0.08)\" stroke=\"rgba(52,211,153,0.2)\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n  <text x=\"398\" y=\"234\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#34D399\" font-size=\"9\" font-family=\"ui-monospace,monospace\">cache-pod (100m)</text>\n  <text x=\"400\" y=\"276\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"rgba(52,211,153,0.55)\" font-size=\"8.5\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">CPU: 4 cores · Memory: 16Gi</text>\n  <text x=\"400\" y=\"288\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"rgba(52,211,153,0.45)\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">properly sized · GPU affinity set</text>\n  <rect x=\"550\" y=\"164\" width=\"230\" height=\"130\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"rgba(52,211,153,0.04)\" stroke=\"rgba(52,211,153,0.25)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" filter=\"url(#glow5)\"/>\n  <text x=\"665\" y=\"180\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"rgba(52,211,153,0.6)\" font-size=\"9\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"700\">Node 3 — Karpenter Spot</text>\n  <rect x=\"562\" y=\"186\" width=\"206\" height=\"24\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"rgba(52,211,153,0.1)\" stroke=\"rgba(52,211,153,0.3)\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n  <text x=\"665\" y=\"202\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#34D399\" font-size=\"9\" font-family=\"ui-monospace,monospace\">burst-pod · burst-pod · burst-pod</text>\n  <text x=\"665\" y=\"232\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"rgba(52,211,153,0.55)\" font-size=\"8.5\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Provisioned in 30s on demand</text>\n  <text x=\"665\" y=\"245\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"rgba(52,211,153,0.45)\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">g4dn.xlarge (GPU) for ML inference</text>\n  <text x=\"665\" y=\"276\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"rgba(52,211,153,0.6)\" font-size=\"8.5\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Spot savings: 60-70% vs On-Demand</text>\n  <text x=\"665\" y=\"288\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"rgba(52,211,153,0.45)\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Consolidation enabled: 40% fewer nodes</text>\n</svg>\n<p class=\"blog-nexus-diagram__caption\">A production Kubernetes cluster with proper separation of concerns: HPA for CPU/memory-based scaling, KEDA for event-driven workloads (queue depth, Kafka lag), and Karpenter for intelligent node provisioning. The most expensive mistake we see: resource limits unset on worker pods (Node 1, yellow), leading to noisy-neighbor OOMKills and $180+/month in idle compute.</p>\n</div><p>When a team says they're having problems with Kubernetes, nine times out of ten the conversation that follows reveals they are having problems with their application. Kubernetes is the magnifying glass that makes those problems visible — but it did not cause them.</p><div class=\"blog-table-wrapper\"><table class=\"blog-comparison-table\"><thead><tr><th>Capability</th><th>Cluster Autoscaler</th><th>Karpenter</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Instance selection</td><td>From pre-configured node groups only</td><td class=\"winner\">Dynamic — any instance type in real time</td></tr><tr><td>Cost optimization</td><td>Baseline</td><td class=\"winner\">20–35% lower on mixed workloads</td></tr><tr><td>Scale-up latency</td><td>2–5 minutes</td><td class=\"winner\">30–90 seconds</td></tr><tr><td>Spot handling</td><td>Manual node group config</td><td class=\"winner\">Native spot fallback, automatic rebalance</td></tr><tr><td>Consolidation</td><td>Node group limits apply</td><td class=\"winner\">Consolidates to fewest nodes automatically</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h2>The FinOps Reality: What Idle Pods Actually Cost</h2><p>The most common FinOps finding: clusters where 30-50% of provisioned compute capacity is chronically idle — not because of traffic variability, but because of misconfigured resource requests. A production cluster analyzed recently had 140 pods with CPU requests set to 1000m. Actual CPU utilization: average 85m, P95 210m. The cluster was provisioned with 140 cores to service a workload peaking at 30 cores — approximately $9,400/month wasted on unused reserved capacity.</p><h2>HPA vs KEDA: Choosing the Right Autoscaling Strategy</h2><p>HPA scales pod replicas based on CPU — fails for event-driven workloads where queue depth determines scale. KEDA extends autoscaling with 50+ event source scalers (SQS depth, Kafka lag, Redis list length). KEDA's scale-to-zero capability is the most impactful cost optimization for batch workloads idle 80% of the time.</p><h2>The Resource Request Anti-Pattern Catalog</h2><ol><li>CPU limits set equal to requests — causes throttling even when the node has idle capacity.</li><li>Memory limits set below typical working set — OOM-kills under load.</li><li>Identical requests and limits across all environments — staging doesn't need production allocation.</li><li>No PodDisruptionBudgets on critical services — node drain can terminate all replicas simultaneously.</li></ol>"
